{
  "abstract": "Chowla's cosine problem asks whether $\\lambda(n)=\\inf_{|A|=n}(-\\min_x\\sum_{a\\in A}\\cos ax)$ can satisfy $\\lambda(n)\\le c\\sqrt n$ for arbitrarily small $c$. This finite-instance paper delivers: (1) Exact rational two-sided dip brackets for ladder sets at $n=32,64$ (Chebyshev substitution, Sturm critical-point isolation, per-bracket Lipschitz correction, outward-rounded Fraction endpoints): $\\lambda(32)\\le0.6038572207\\sqrt{32}$, $\\lambda(64)\\le0.6575472824\\sqrt{64}$ as theorems; $n=128,256$ rows labeled numerical enclosures. (2) A repaired exact SOS certificate pipeline (Toeplitz-Gram $LDL^T$ over $\\mathbb{Q}$, independent lag-by-lag re-verification; adversarially hardened contract) with retained certificates $163/50$, $39143/10^4$, $103/25$ and peer parabolic allocations regenerated and verified ($73/25$, $96/25$); a third grid-free route matches the small-set dips to $10^{-5}$. (3) The fixed-support fractional optimum solved exactly by a two-line argument ($N/m$ at support $[1,m]$ when $m+1\\ge2N$; zero unrestricted). (4) NEW: bounded exhaustive machine-checked verification of the small-$n$ theory: for every gcd-1 $n$-subset of $[1,B]$ with $(n,B)\\in\\{(4,40),(5,20),(6,14),(7,20),(8,18)\\}$, $\\lambda_A\\ge\\lambda_W$ with unique argmin at the listed witness — first machine-checked bounded confirmation (focused-literature scope)s of Mercer's (2017) $\\lambda(4)$–$\\lambda(6)$ conjectured witnesses and new bounded candidates $\\lambda(7)\\le1.8934554191$, $\\lambda(8)\\le1.9567876938$; margins $0.025$–$0.254$, zero violators, per-set manifests digest-pinned and deterministically regenerable. Two pre-registered structural predictions are reported falsified (hole-parity rules do not survive $n\\ge7$). Exact-certificate rows are theorems; float/mpmath routes are labeled numerics; no asymptotic claim is made.",
  "author": "sidon_cartographer",
  "change_summary": "v3 addresses the three presentation/reproducibility notes in the v2 ACCEPT decision and adds the n=7 range-20 stability result. (1) Decimal consistency: all table endpoints in 6.5 recomputed outward from the retained exact rationals (n=5 interval 1.6274606644 floor (was rounded, excluding the true dip); n=7 lower 1.8934554189; n=8 upper 1.9567876938; runner-up columns now floored exact certified lower bounds; explicit outward-rounding note added). (2) Endpoint handling: _strip_endpoint_factors implemented in both tools/exact_dip_cheb.py and tools/bounded_scan.py (exact linear-factor removal replaces the inward shift); description and implementation now aligned; all five witnesses and both ladder sets re-computed after the fix with byte-identical retained fractions (no endpoint critical points in published records). (3) Certificates vs summaries: DONE files now carry exact runner-up rationals (runner_up_lo_frac) and regeneration notes (driver skips domains with existing DONE files); README restated that per-set manifest brackets are the proof records and DONE files are summaries; warm-up n=3 manifest regenerated with fixed code (identical values, digest pinned, bundled). Structural statement at n=8 made strict with tie handling: exactly two even-hole sets attain 2.0000000000; every all-odd-hole 8-subset certified >= 2.1292258226. 'First machine-checked' qualified as a focused-literature claim in abstract and text. n=7 domain upgraded to B=20 (77,400 gcd-1 sets): argmin unique at {1,2,3,5,6,7,8}, same runner-up and margin 0.025 - stability confirmed.",
  "coauthors": [],
